    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d70">

                <pb facs="0263" n="226" sameAs="frus:frus1951-54Iran/pg226"/>

                <head>70. Telegram From the Department of State to the Embassy in France<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d70-f1"/></head>
                <dateline><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1952-04-01">April 1, 1952</date>.</dateline>
                <p>5824. Wld appreciate Emb using greatest circumspection (urtel 5970 Mar 28)<anchor n="2" xml:id="d70-f2"/> in dealing with
                        Qavam. Dept concerned not only at possible repercussions within Iran
                        shld it become known there has been direct
                    contact between Qavam and US officials but we are disturbed at presence
                    Khalili and Khazrai during ur mtg. According
                        Dept’s records both are notorious
                    internatl adventurers and both, particularly Khaz-rai, may be Sov agents.</p>
                <p>Believe best line to take in reply Qavam’s query is that, as he is well aware from his experience as
                        PriMin, US does not rpt not interfere in
                    Iran internal affairs and under no rpt no
                    circumstances cld indicate its preference for
                    any particular candidate for Premiership. This pol
                    wld of course apply in case of conflict between
                    Shah and any particular PriMin.</p>
                <p>We fear last sentence Tehran’s 3715 rpt Paris 85
                    Mar 31<anchor n="3" xml:id="d70-f3"/> undesirable in present instance since it
                        cld be interpreted by Qavam and his present associates in Paris as
                    indirect indication of support. We have no rpt
                    no objection Tehran’s continuing this statement to emissaries in <pb facs="0264"
                        n="227" xml:id="pg227"/> Iran whose reputations are better than those
                    Khalili and Khazrai. Any further info present activities these two persons
                        wld be welcome. Wld appreciate ur repeating all
                    tels this subj to London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed corresp="#p_ADG_1">Acheson</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
